// Module 11 quiz - Deep Learning for AI Startups
$CATEGORY: $course$/Module 11

::M11 Q1:: What should the first capstone build be? {
~Every feature at once
=The thinnest end-to-end version#A thin version that runs from a real input to a real output shows you where the surprises are while there is still time to fix them.
~Only the pitch slides
~A new framework
}

::M11 Q2:: Why test with real users early? {
~To avoid evaluation
~To add parameters
~To delay deployment
=To learn what actually matters before over-investing#Real users show you which problems matter, before you spend weeks polishing the wrong thing.
}

::M11 Q3:: When is it reasonable to use a pretrained model or API? {
=Usually, unless you have a clear reason to train your own#Pretrained models and APIs are the cheapest, fastest start. Train your own only when measurements show that you must.
~Never
~Only for toy projects
~Only when you have no data
}

::M11 Q4:: In a team, what should be agreed first? {
~Slide fonts
~Team logo
=Interfaces between components#If everyone agrees the inputs and outputs of each part first, the parts will fit together when they are joined.
~The final grade
}

::M11 Q5:: What does a must-have versus nice-to-have list help with? {
~Increasing model size
~Removing tests
~Avoiding users
=Controlling scope within limited time#It protects the essential work, and decides in advance what to drop when time runs short.
}
